@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] ferry-authoritative-route-data
The production ferry MUST be one ship shuttling between Hidamari and Brinecove. Its runtime path,
arrival/departure manoeuvres, boarding endpoints and world cuts MUST come from the same source-bound
data checked against the final exported world. Missing seabed, failed audits and stale source or
export identities MUST refuse production generation and import. The normal build and packaging graph
MUST include the preparation, access cut, import and runtime staging.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] ferry-natural-motion
Production ferry manoeuvres and sea crossings MUST sail continuous boat trajectories with no pivoting
in place (yaw rate <= 3 deg/s and zero yaw while |speed| < 0.5 m/s), lateral drift speed <= 0.3 m/s
everywhere (<= 0.5 m/s within 10 m of a berth), turn radius >= 3 hull lengths (240 m) at sea and >= 1
hull length (80 m) at <= 2.0 m/s in harbour, curved astern legs at <= 1.5 m/s for at most 1.5 hull
lengths (120 m) separated from ahead legs by a full stop with zero yaw, and a straight aligned final
approach of at least 15 m into each berth.
